senses.gloss:
Roruka (var. Rauruka), nt. (= Pali Roruka),
(1) n. of a town, capital of the Sauvīras (Pali Sov˚): Mv 〔iii.208.18〕; home of Rudrāyaṇa, Divy 〔544.23 ff.〕; in 〔545.26〕 (mss.), and usually later in the story (〔550.1—11〕; 〔551.6〕; 〔552.17 ff.〕; 〔556.16 ff.〕; 〔559.4〕; 〔563.12 ff.〕), called Rauruka;
(2) n. of a city in the south (and so apparently not the same as 1, which is in the northwest): Gv 〔453.18, 25〕.
